    "<!--\n",
    "TODO: awaiting guidance. Includes the limitations that should be stated\n",
    "before a referee states them.\n",
    "\n",
    "Proposed scope:\n",
    "\n",
    "  - Do survey clicks measure anything real? Clicking is nearly free, so\n",
    "    estimated search-cost LEVELS will not transfer to the field. Mitigations\n",
    "    to weigh: incentive alignment, artificial latency, an explicit click\n",
    "    budget, a time-denominated cost. Fallback: relative and comparative\n",
    "    statements transfer even when levels do not — which is the standing\n",
    "    defense of conjoint utilities, so it is defensible ground. Say it before\n",
    "    a reviewer does.\n",
    "  - Rational expectations about the unopened alternative. Weitzman requires\n",
    "    the respondent to know the distribution behind each click, which she does\n",
    "    not at the start of a survey. Implies a practice block, and possibly\n",
    "    modeling learning across tasks.\n",
    "  - Do respondents follow the reservation rule? The lab literature says\n",
    "    partially (@sec-lit-lab). Report fit against a satisficing alternative.\n",
    "  - Thin identification at commercial task counts.\n",
    "  - Where conjoint remains the right tool: feature-level willingness-to-pay\n",
    "    for a defined bundle, new-product configuration with nothing to search,\n",
    "    orthogonal designs for clean part-worths, mature share simulators,\n",
    "    categories with no list-screen, and any study where established norms and\n",
    "    benchmarks matter more than a new method.\n",
    "  - Extensions: filters and sorts as search actions [@Chen_Yao_2017],\n",
    "    discovery of alternatives [@Greminger_2022], search across sessions.\n",
    "-->"
   ],
